H1770.strongs:
Origin: denominative from 1709;
Meaning: to fish
KJV renders: fish.

H1771.strongs:
Origin: from 1770;
Meaning: a fisherman
KJV renders: fisher.

H1772.strongs:
Origin: intensive from 1675;
Meaning: a falcon (from its rapid flight)
KJV renders: vulture.

H1773.strongs:
Origin: of uncertain derivation;
Meaning: ink
KJV renders: ink.

H1774.strongs:
Origin: as if from 1768 and 2091; of gold;
Meaning: Dizahab, a place in the Desert
KJV renders: Dizahab.

H1775.strongs:
Origin: perhaps for 1769;
Meaning: Dimon, a place in Palestine
KJV renders: Dimon.

H1776.strongs:
Origin: feminine of 1775;
Meaning: Dimonah, a place in Palestine
KJV renders: Dimonah.

H1777.strongs:
Origin: or (Genesis 6:3) דּוּן; a primitive root;
Meaning: to rule; by implication to judge (as umpire); also to strive (as at law)
KJV renders: contend contend execute (judgment) judge minister judgment plead (the cause) at strife strive.

H1778.strongs:
Origin: (Aramaic) corresponding to 1777;
Meaning: to judge
KJV renders: judge.

H1779.strongs:
Origin: or (Job 19:29) דּוּן; from 1777;
Meaning: judgement (the suit, justice, sentence or tribunal); by implication also strife
KJV renders: cause, judgement, plea, strife.

H1781.strongs:
Origin: from 1777;
Meaning: a judge or advocate
KJV renders: judge.

H1783.strongs:
Origin: feminine of 1779; justice;
Meaning: Dinah, the daughter of Jacob
KJV renders: Dinah.

H1784.strongs:
Origin: (Aramaic) partial from uncertain primitive;
Meaning: a Dinaite or inhabitant of some unknown Assyria province
KJV renders: Dinaite.

H1785.strongs:
Origin: from a root corresp. to 1751;
Meaning: a battering-tower
KJV renders: fort.

H1786.strongs:
Origin: from 1758;
Meaning: threshing-time
KJV renders: threshing.

H1787.strongs:
Origin: Diyshon, the same as 1788;
Meaning: Dishon, the name of two Edomites
KJV renders: Dishon.

H1788.strongs:
Origin: from 1758;
Meaning: the leaper, i.e. an antelope
KJV renders: pygarg.

H1790.strongs:
Origin: from an unused root (compare 1794);
Meaning: crushed, i.e. (figuratively) injured
KJV renders: afflicted, oppressed.

H1791.strongs:
Origin: (Aramaic) or דָּךְ; (Aramaic), prolonged from 1668;
Meaning: this
KJV renders: the same, this.

H1792.strongs:
Origin: a primitive root (compare 1794);
Meaning: to crumble; transitively, to bruise (literally or figuratively)
KJV renders: beat to pieces, break (in pieces), bruise, contrite, crush, destroy, humble, oppress, smite.

H1793.strongs:
Origin: from 1792;
Meaning: crushed (literally powder, or figuratively, contrite)
KJV renders: contrite, destruction.

H1794.strongs:
Origin: a primitive root (compare 1790, 1792);
Meaning: to collapse (phys. or mentally)
KJV renders: break (sore), contrite, crouch.

H1795.strongs:
Origin: from 1794 like 1793;
Meaning: mutilated
KJV renders: wounded.

H1796.strongs:
Origin: from 1794;
Meaning: a dashing of surf
KJV renders: wave.

H1797.strongs:
Origin: (Aramaic) prolonged from 1791;
Meaning: this
KJV renders: same, that, this.

H1798.strongs:
Origin: (Aramaic) corresponding to 2145;
Meaning: properly, a male, i.e. of sheep
KJV renders: ram.

H1799.strongs:
Origin: (Aramaic) or דׇּכְרָן (Aramaic); corresponding to 2146;
Meaning: a register
KJV renders: record.
